        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Yes! The idea is to allow the plugin to do `v<A-l><Esc>` by just pressing `<A-l>` with any `v:count`, which is a bit more ergonomic and aligns with the behaviour I honestly expected from the plugin when I installed it, which I'm sure is the case of others.\r\n\r\nI don't think this would help with dot-repeat, as it currently only repeats the last `P`. I see that `H.make_cmd_normal` disables the command from altering the yank register, so pressing `.` will actually put what was in `\"0` before you pressed `<A-l>`, am I right? Still, for such a small change as is moving a character left or right, I have never reached for the dot to repeat the motionalthough I'm sure someone will consider this absolute heresy :-P",
