        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Yes! The idea is to allow the plugin to do `v<A-l><Esc>` by just pressing `<A-l>` with any `v:count`, which is a bit more ergonomic and aligns with the behaviour I honestly expected from the plugin when I installed it, which I'm sure is the case of others.\r\n\r\nI see. I am afraid, this goes against the whole *linewise* movement. The charwise movement is still suggested to be done via visual mode. The reasoning is that I'd say the most common charwise movement of a single character is by a single column, in which case `xp` works good enough. For more complex cases, visual selection also provides better feedback about the current state of the move.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
