        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I see. Thanks for the well-reasoned feedback :-D\r\n\r\nI ended up using this mapping in my config to make it behave the way I want:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.move\").setup({})\r\n\r\nlocal function move_selection(direction)\r\n    vim.fn.feedkeys(\"v\", \"nx\")\r\n    MiniMove.move_selection(direction)\r\n    vim.fn.feedkeys(\"v\", \"nx\")\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<A-h>\", function () move_selection(\"left\")  end, {noremap = true})\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<A-l>\", function () move_selection(\"right\") end, {noremap = true})\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy goal with the PR was to offer the community a solution in case they had a need similar to mine. This is the second best solution, so if anyone comes looking for this, they can yank this snippet ;-) Again, thank you for your work! This wouldn't have been possible if you hadn't made your plugins so easy to integrate from the outside.\r\n\r\nSee you around in the interwebs!",
